[
{
"id": "u04114",
"e": "      <p class=\"hint\">Of the 44,796 inscriptions from Rome in EDR, 42,722 have a readable text in the data set. Using a dictionary of 127 Latin occupational titles we found an occupation in 2,338 inscriptions: physicians, cooks, goldsmiths, accountants. The inscriptions of soldiers (2,171) are left out of this summary, as are priesthoods and senatorial and equestrian offices. Every hit was checked by reading, and those where the word is not the person’s occupation were dropped: for example the emperors’ victory title “Medicus”, the names Mercator, Sutorius or Fullonius, the divine name “Bona Dea Nutrix”, and the texts of laws and decrees. EDR does not yet contain all the inscriptions of Rome, so the figures show proportions, not complete head counts.</p>"
},
