"e": "          <tr><td><a href=\"#\" data-goto=\"csalario\">The Salarian cemetery</a></td><td class=\"pn\">2,608</td><td class=\"pn\">75 (2.9%)</td><td>steward (8), physician (6), public scribe (5), gladiator (5)</td></tr>"
},
{
"id": "u04510",
"e": "      <li><b>Occupations in the inscriptions.</b> Data: EDR (see “Inscriptions”). The summary is our own: a search for 127 Latin occupational titles in the texts of the inscriptions, grouped into nine sectors; every hit checked by reading (excluded items: occ/excl.py); legal status from case-agreeing markers in the name belonging to the title; military inscriptions and second copies of repeated inscriptions excluded; addresses from the place given after the title (occ/lex.py, occ/calc.py). The standard study of the subject: Sandra R. Joshel, <i>Work, Identity, and Legal Status at Rome. A Study of the Occupational Inscriptions</i>, Norman–London 1992.</li>"
}
]